# Verification-first (kmp-ble)

Quality is proven by evidence, not by following this rule alone. See [ADR-0002](docs/adr/ADR-0002-verification-first-agent-assisted-development.md).

## Before declaring work done

1. Read [docs/verification/matrix.md](docs/verification/matrix.md) and run every command for surfaces you touched.
2. Attach evidence: test output, build logs, or a short verification note.
3. Do **not** mark complete on compile-only when behavior or public API changed.
4. Do **not** claim physical BLE / GATT Lab E2E (human-only; see `TESTING.md`).

## Routing shortcuts

| Touched | Run |
| --- | --- |
| Core `commonMain` (non-concurrency) | `./gradlew iosSimulatorArm64Test --no-daemon` (add `jvmTest` if state machine / queue / observations) |
| GATT queue, peripheral concurrency | `./gradlew jvmTest --no-daemon` |
| `androidMain` / quirks host | `./gradlew testAndroidHostTest --no-daemon` |
| Android device tests | `./gradlew connectedAndroidDeviceTest --no-daemon` |
| `iosMain` / apple | `./gradlew compileKotlinIosSimulatorArm64 iosSimulatorArm64Test --no-daemon` |
| `kmp-ble-profiles` / `dfu` / `codec*` | Matching `:module:allTests` (see matrix) |
| Samples | Mirror CI `sample` compile tasks |

## Out of scope for agents (human-only)

- Editing `.github/workflows/**` or other protected policy / branch-protection files
- Physical BLE hardware verification
- Public API / new module / expect-actual boundary changes without an ADR or Gary approval
- Adding Maestro / mobile-mcp / Castly-style secret hooks unless a later ADR says so

Do not duplicate CI policy here; L2 enforces merge gates.
